  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "IMO, the Trust System isn't very good at filtering nuisance people. Instead, I use the Trust settings to block non-friends, simply for all around performance increases (I'm sure I'm not the only one); and just manually filter annoyances if need be. \n\nIt would be amazing if, instead of filtering avatars by their account's Trust Level, to instead (or have the addition to) filter models based on their Avatar Performance. With friends being an exception of course. It would allow the best of both worlds, as you wouldn't have to rely on the Trust settings as a crutch to gain FPS instead of using it for it's true purpose. It would allow a higher degree of control over the content that you want, or don't want to see in VRChat. \n\nBeing able to filter models by Avatar Performance and Trust would help greatly in performance. As of now, the only easily accessible options to increase performance in busy worlds are to block everyone's avatars not on your friends list, picking and choosing manually who to see; or to allow all avatars by default and manually block laggy avatars. For me, the latter takes a lot of time to do, and in any laggy lobby it would be a pain. Avatar Performance filtering would fix all of that.\n\nA point of controversy with the Trust system, was that newer players might be out-casted as a result of people having their avatars blocked by default, simply for performance reasons. Filtering by Avatar Performance would allow newer players to have a chance, if they are a talented creator, or won't be a performance hinderer to you; which is THE only reason I have newer players blocked by default to be honest. If this option was in addition to the Trust System, you could still choose to block newer player's avatars if you didn't trust them as well. \n\n",
